---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import aboutPhoto from '../assets/site/about-tim.jpg';
---

<PageLayout
	title="About"
	heading="Howdy!"
	description="Tim O'Connell makes colorful, stenciled, one-of-a-kind ceramics out of the Throw & Build studio in Wallingford, Seattle."
>
	<div class="layout">
		<div class="photo">
			<Picture
				src={aboutPhoto}
				alt="Tim O'Connell leaning on a wooden fence at a green coastal overlook, pointing at the camera"
				widths={[400, 800, 1200]}
				sizes="(min-width: 768px) 40vw, 100vw"
				formats={['avif', 'webp']}
				fallbackFormat="jpg"
				loading="eager"
			/>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				I'm Tim. I am from Seattle, currently live in Seattle and make my ceramic artwork in Seattle.
				Currently working out of the Throw &amp; Build studio in Wallingford, I have varied interests
				within the ceramics world, but my favorite pots are colorful, large, stenciled, one-of-a-kind
				pieces.
			</p>
			<p>
				My ceramics journey began in high school at Shorewood High School in Shoreline, WA. I took a
				ceramics class and instantly fell in love with the wheel. No idea why it spoke to me so, but I
				was hooked. I still have my first ever pot. I then moved on to take ceramics classes at
				Shoreline CC (now called Shoreline College) and studied under the great Sam Scott.
			</p>
			<p>
				As time went on, ceramics came in and out of my life over the next two decades. A pop-up studio
				here, random class there. I never really focused on it in full again until late 2025. I now
				spend roughly 20 hours a week working on the craft (yes, still have a day job, booooooooo), and
				who knows how much time when I am not being held back by the man.
			</p>
			<p>
				I usually work in light clay colors, though I do love black clays. Laguna B-Mix is probably my
				current favorite clay to work with, but I stray into all types of porcelains and occasionally
				black clays as well. I love working with stencils that I create on my own and print with a
				Cricut machine. I do not love the Cricut machine, but it does help me make some amazing pots.
			</p>
			<p>
				You'll find vases, mugs, planters, a bolo or two, pitchers and freakishly decorated pots of all
				sizes often with a lot of underglazes as I attempt to figure out what "my style" ultimately is.
			</p>
			<p>
				Thanks for checking out the page. Feel free to email me at
				<a href="mailto:timoconn@pm.me">timoconn@pm.me</a> with questions and check the
				<a href="/faq">FAQ</a> for basic questions.
			</p>
			<p>Cheers!! — Tim</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.layout {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-5);
	}

	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.layout {
			grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
			align-items: start;
		}
	}

	.photo :global(img) {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	.prose p {
		margin-block: 0 var(--space-3);
	}
</style>
